{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0900"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c075): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c075.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0900"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/games","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__games.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1018],["+","The genre's later revival came from Germany. The Hamburg studio Daedalic Entertainment released Deponia in 2012, the story of the lazy, self-satisfied inventor Rufus, who longs to escape a planet that serves as a rubbish dump. Its sequel, Chaos on Deponia, followed in October 2012, and Goodbye Deponia completed the trilogy in 2013.\n\n"],["=",129]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",984],["+","Die spätere Wiederbelebung des Genres kam aus Deutschland. Das Hamburger Studio Daedalic Entertainment veröffentlichte 2012 Deponia, die Geschichte des faulen, selbstgefälligen Erfinders Rufus, der von einem Planeten fliehen will, der als Müllhalde dient. Die Fortsetzung Chaos auf Deponia folgte im Oktober 2012, und Goodbye Deponia schloss die Trilogie 2013 ab.\n\n"],["=",129]]}]},
